{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfn8l1hpiw","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"OVERRIDE: note to note kept context edge cannot drive structBoost over HTTP","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: the CL adapter's edge keep/prune verdict is faithful but its retrieval effect is INERT for note↔note edges over the current daemon HTTP surface. Two daemon-side causes, both verified 2026-06-15: (1) buildGraph (daemon.js ~L1612) pushes note nodes with a hardcoded context_deps: [], and the structBoost reranker (routes/graph.js ~L363-396) builds adjacency only from node.context_deps — so a kept note→note edge never enters the adjacency and structBoost stays 0 no matter the verdict; (2) overlayStore.save (lib/overlay.js ~L262-264) only emits edge_added for edges whose signature is NOT already in prev.edges, so keepEdge's in-place promotion of an existing autowire edge (judged:false→true, weight:0→score) is NOT persisted for a non-live (isolated eval) workspace — /judge/verdict returns kept:1 but reload shows weight:0. NET: keepEdge/pruneEdge post and journal correctly, but the only DEMONSTRABLE retrieval lever the judge controls is the dup-cluster decision (markDistinct makes a near-dup note retrieval-visible; consolidate supersedes it, pruned from retrieval). Clean fix (gated, restart-required): give note nodes real context_deps from kept edges + emit an edge-update event on in-place promotion.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T20:06:15.173Z","vec":[-0.1090560331940651,0.028088968247175217,-0.04971424117684364,0.021261174231767654,0.09373944997787476,-0.01230285968631506,-0.008546614088118076,0.006649293005466461,-0.034633684903383255,-0.004238918889313936,0.02635575644671917,0.01110461913049221,-0.0028350346256047487,-0.03266667574644089,0.0026917760260403156,0.04579422250390053,0.07548774033784866,-0.020284349098801613,-0.02762870490550995,-0.021694401279091835,0.03941992297768593,-0.0026591122150421143,0.043512724339962006,-0.012734407559037209,0.007784